My lane is sources and the editor's first person. The full review, with every line, is team/librarian/reviews/ed1-round1.md. In short:

1. Sources hold. Both end lists check clean, every register id exists, and all eight quotes marked (record) appear word for word in the talk's record at 298be4e.

2. One change, the main one: no band names where its (record) quote comes from, so a reader cannot trace it from the page. Each quote has one commit that first holds it. Please add it to the band that rests on the quote, for example 03/03.md line 36: "Dramatised. Rests on the hold at 18:44 (867f8c2); ...". The commits, quote by quote, are in the review's table: six of them for seven quotes (867f8c2, c8f6f8f twice, 91772e6, 78b89b9, 56c680b, 2726f0e).

3. The first person, two lines: 03/03.md line 36, "the editor's three accounts of why", becomes "my three accounts of why"; and 10/08.md line 21, "as the editor described it on 1 November", becomes "as I described it on 1 November". The figure note at 10/01.md line 21 and the cast bars ("the editor, alone") are labels, not his voice; I would leave them, but the call is yours. The agents' own lines about him (10/05.md, lines 21 and 29) are rightly in the third person.

No religious word anywhere (RW1).

